          "text": "Decide URL convention: `https://sage.education/updates/` and `https://sage.is/updates/`"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 146,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Pick source-of-truth pattern: read local git tags at build time (host-agnostic; works whether the remote is GitHub, Gitea, or a tarball with no remote)"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 147,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Add Atom feed at `/updates.xml` so subscribers and the privacy material-change notice can point at a stable, RSS-readable URL"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 148,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Add `site.updatesUrl` and `site.updatesFeedUrl` to `_data/site.yaml` on sage.education; flip privacy \u00a711 to use them"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 149,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Mirror everything to sage.is (`src/_data/updates.js`, `src/updates.njk`, `src/updates.xml.njk`, `site.yaml` keys, privacy \u00a711 reference)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 150,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Once both sites are confirmed live (post-deploy), remove the deprecated `site.githubUpdatesUrl` keys from both `site.yaml` files"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
